  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 PM EST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\n***Tonight Through Sunday Night***\n\nUpper level ridging will continue to move into the region from the \nwest bringing high pressure to the forecast area. Calm conditions \nand clear skies tonight will effectively cool temperatures into the \nupper 20s and low 30s. Winds will remain light (under 10 mph)and \npredominantly out of the north tomorrow. Sunny skies are here to \nstick around with high temperatures in the upper 40s and low 50s for \nthe rest of the weekend. Nighttime lows will continue in the upper \n20s and low 30s for Sunday night. Some patchy valley fog will be \npossible tomorrow morning, but is not expected to have substantial \nimpacts. \n\n***Monday Through The End Of The Week***\n\nAs we move into the beginning of the work week, the surface high \npressure strengthens (over 1030mb) and will move directly over the \nOhio Valley. This will bring a wind shift on Tuesday from the NE to \nthe SE, which will help promote some warming. Temperatures will \nbegin to increase daily as we stay in this pattern in the extended \nperiod. High temperatures from Tuesday through the end of the period \nare within the 90th percentile of climatology. Afternoon highs are \nexpected to be in the mid to upper 50s for Monday and Tuesday, with \na 60-70% chance of breaking 60 on Wednesday. By late next week, \nmajority of the area will see 70 degrees. Nighttime temperatures \nwill continue to see efficient cooling due to light winds and clear \nskies overnight. Low temperatures will remain in the 20s and 30s for \nthe first half of the week, while the later half will see low 40s. \nDry conditions will continue through the end of the forecast period \nas high pressure persist.",
